<title>FRANCE: U.S top country of origin for Paris Oct 96 imports.</title>
<headline>U.S top country of origin for Paris Oct 96 imports.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United States was the principal country of origin for import traffic handled at the Paris airports in October 1996, Paris airport authority, Aeroports de Paris (ADP), figures show.</p>
<p>The 20 leading countries of origin for ADP imports in October 1996, with percentage change on October 1995, in parentheses, were as follows:</p>
<p> 1  United States	    12,904 tonnes down  2.3pct</p>
<p> 2  India			 2,585 tonnes up   29.8</p>
<p> 3  Hong Kong		   2,201 tonnes up    8.2</p>
<p> 4  Japan			 2,082 tonnes down 11.6</p>
<p> 5  Canada			2,006 tonnes down 16.8</p>
<p> 6 United Kingdom	     1,794 tonnes up    4.8</p>
<p> 7 Germany			1,618 tonnes up   73.4</p>
<p> 8 Italy			  1,126 tonnes down  1.3</p>
<p> 9  Thailand			889 tonnes down 18.4</p>
<p> 10  Kenya			  854 tonnes down  6.9</p>
<p> 11 China			   737 tonnes up   66.4</p>
<p> 12 Argentina		     648 tonnes up   14.7</p>
<p> 13 South Africa		  558 tonnes down  6.0</p>
<p> 14 United Arab Emirates	520 tonnes down 22.7</p>
<p> 15 Singapore		     499 tonnes down 22.1</p>
<p> 16 Israel			  463 tonnes down 20.3</p>
<p> 17 French West Indies	  454 tonnes down  3.1</p>
<p> 18 Morocco			 430 tonnes down  6.6</p>
<p> 19 Brazil			  419 tonnes down 17.4</p>
<p> 20 Switzerland		   409 tonnes down 10.4</p>
<p> Total			   33,196 tonnes</p>
<p>Global October 1996  import traffic to the  Paris airports, Charles de Gaulle and Orly, totalled 45,113 tonnes, an increase of 1.7 percent on the same month last year, ADP said. - Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+44 171 542 5017</p>
